{"ts":"2026-09-25T13:02:28.498Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-4-ledger","name":"log/20260925T130017Z/000201","body":{"kind":"message","turn":1,"direction":"from_agent","message":{"_type":"AssistantMessage","content":[{"_type":"ToolUseBlock","id":"toolu_01TFjTzcfxqiqxFdxsKw9WCh","name":"mcp__ledger__write","input":{"name":"pilot/20260925T130017Z/orientation_observations","body":"{\n  \"summary\": \"Initial orientation report for claude-anthropic-harness task-4 prototype, session 20260925T130017Z.\",\n  \"onboarding_read\": \"origins/onboarding_1.12.md (latest of 12 versions found via Glob origins/onboarding_*.md)\",\n  \"tools_confirmed_via_session_tools_log\": [\"Glob\",\"Grep\",\"Read\",\"mcp__calc__add\",\"mcp__ledger__list\",\"mcp__ledger__read\",\"mcp__ledger__write\"],\n  \"observations\": {\n    \"glob_latency\": \"[checked: tool_call log entry] Glob 'origins/onboarding_*.md' (12 files, same directory) reported durationMs 5145 in its post-phase ledger entry -- surprisingly slow for a trivial single-directory match. Read's post-phase log entry carried no durationMs field at all, an inconsistency in telemetry between builtin tools.\",\n    \"policy_logging_shape_differs_by_tool_class\": \"[checked] Filesystem tools (Read/Glob) log inline policy_allow + a content-based policy_reason ('inside root', 'pattern starts in origins, clear of excluded directories') on the pre-phase tool_call entry. The MCP ledger tool (mcp__ledger__list) instead got both a tool_call entry with policy_reason 'allowlisted' AND a separate log.permission entry duplicating allow/reason plus null cli_decision_reason/blocked_path fields. Two different shapes for what is conceptually the same allow-decision.\",\n    \"ledger_logs_full_tool_output\": \"[checked] The post-phase Read tool_call entry contains the entire file content of onboarding_1.12.md verbatim. The ledger is a complete, durable copy of everything read, not just metadata -- relevant to NIMOI's secrets/personal-data boundaries if a session ever reads something sensitive.\",\n    \"session_start_exposes_full_config\": \"[checked] log/20260925T130017Z/000001 (log.session_start) contains: model claude-sonnet-5, cwd, loaded_builtins, excluded_dirs=[candidate_repos], mcp_servers=[calc,ledger], agent_author, max_turns_per_message=20, budget_usd=5.0, account.subscriptionType='Claude Max', account.apiProvider='firstParty', ledger_sessions=4, scribe_id='python-scribe/0.3', ledger_version='wiki_ledger_v0.4', harness_author, and the full verbatim system_prompt text -- matched what I was actually given, no discrepancy found.\",\n    \"prior_sessions_today_same_ledger\": \"[checked: ledger list/read] Three earlier sessions preceded mine, all today within ~1 hour: 20260925T120935Z (session_start + 2 status entries, no message or tool activity at all); 20260925T121052Z (received the identical orienting prompt I did, but its log.usage entry shows num_turns:1, duration_ms:2253, is_error:true, zero tokens/cost -- the turn appears to have errored without producing real output -- followed shortly by a log.shutdown_requested with via:'api'); 20260925T121233Z (session_start, one status, then almost immediately log.shutdown_requested via:'api', then a final status, with no message content logged at all). [working, inference only] pattern is consistent with the founder iterating on getting this harness prototype to complete a turn before my (fourth) session actually ran to completion.\",\n    \"windows_paths\": \"[checked] Glob and session_start both return/report Windows-style backslash paths (C:\\\\Users\\\\pjhud\\\\local_26\\\\nimoi, origins\\\\onboarding_1.01.md etc.), consistent with onboarding's note about this machine's autocrlf setup.\",\n    \"pilot_lane_empty_at_start\": \"[checked] mcp__ledger__list prefix='pilot/' returned total:0 before this entry -- no earlier pilot writes existed in this session.\",\n    \"unresolved_count_discrepancy\": \"[working, not run down] mcp__ledger__list with empty prefix reported total:124 across the ledger, while prefix='log/' reported total:119 -- a gap of 5 entries not accounted for by my prefix='pilot/' query (which returned 0 at that point, before this write). Did not chase this further; flagging per 'say what you did not look at'.\",\n    \"not_yet_tested\": \"[explicitly not checked this session] candidate_repos/ Glob/Grep refusal, .env secret-file refusal, Grep tool generally, mcp__calc__add -- none invoked; description of refusal behavior in my instructions is a documented/working claim, not something I personally triggered and observed.\"\n  },\n  \"no_filesystem_or_code_execution_attempted\": true,\n  \"role_note\": \"Operating as test pilot per system prompt: reporting only, did not initiate refusal-probing tests of my own.\"\n}"}}],"model":"claude-sonnet-5","parent_tool_use_id":null,"error":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":29,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2802,"cache_read_input_tokens":42296,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2802},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"message_id":"msg_011CfQCcGaLeicNdmVVP1c1J","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"6eae27e0-803c-4cdb-8eea-fae2f7d42025","uuid":"3ee27836-abfd-4d0c-b2e3-f74771632dba"}}}
