{"ts":"2026-09-25T13:02:52.270Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-4-ledger","name":"log/20260925T130017Z/000210","body":{"kind":"message","turn":1,"direction":"harness","message":{"_type":"ResultMessage","subtype":"success","duration_ms":138581,"duration_api_ms":134393,"is_error":false,"num_turns":25,"session_id":"6eae27e0-803c-4cdb-8eea-fae2f7d42025","stop_reason":"end_turn","total_cost_usd":0.9425675,"usage":{"input_tokens":268,"cache_creation_input_tokens":51630,"cache_read_input_tokens":220655,"output_tokens":12584,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":51630,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":29,"output_tokens":2390,"cache_read_input_tokens":45098,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6532,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6532},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"result":"Orientation is done. Here's the full report.\n\n## Orientation\n\nI globbed `origins/onboarding_*.md`, found 12 versions (`1.01` through `1.12`), and read the highest, `origins/onboarding_1.12.md` — dated 2026-09-24, written by the session that audited the pre-bootstrapping work. It's long and heavily self-referential NIMOI doctrine: a \"bar\" concept that must be stated on every brief, a working-claim/checked-claim distinction (which I've adopted below and in my ledger entry), boundaries on untrusted text/secrets/personal data, a virtue-methodology self-optimization convention, and — usefully — a \"Harnesses\" section that explicitly says *\"you may be running in a variant harness under development... if your tools or instructions differ from what this file assumes, say so.\"* That caveat is doing real work here: the onboarding's harness lore covers \"Claude Code\" and \"Codex,\" neither of which is what I'm running in. I have not verified any of the many paths onboarding points to (`nimoi_mapping_project/`, `bootstrap-harness/`, `origins/virtues.md`, etc.) — I read only the one file, as directed (\"onboarding never requires a reading tour\").\n\n## Tools I have, and how they behaved\n\n**Glob / Grep / Read** — read-only, confined to `C:\\Users\\pjhud\\local_26\\nimoi`, per both my system prompt and the ledger's own `session_start` record (`excluded_dirs: [\"candidate_repos\"]`). I used Glob and Read; I have not yet used Grep at all, so I can't report on it firsthand.\n\n- Glob (`origins/onboarding_*.md`) returned 12 filenames with **Windows backslash separators** (`origins\\onboarding_1.01.md`, etc.) — confirms Windows underneath, consistent with onboarding's note about this machine's `core.autocrlf` setting. The ledger's post-phase log for that call reported `durationMs: 5145` — over five seconds to glob one small directory. That's slow for something this trivial; I flag it as surprising and unexplained rather than assume a cause.\n- Read (`origins/onboarding_1.12.md`) succeeded, `policy_reason: \"inside root\"`. Notably, its post-phase ledger log contained **the entire file content verbatim** — the ledger isn't just recording that I read a file, it's making a full durable copy of what I read. Its ledger entry also carried **no timing field**, unlike Glob's — an inconsistency in telemetry between the two builtin tools.\n\n**mcp__calc__add** — available (confirmed in the `session_tools` log entry) but I haven't called it; there was no orienting reason to.\n\n**Ledger tools (`mcp__ledger__read`, `mcp__ledger__list`, `mcp__ledger__write`)** — all worked as described. Two things worth noting:\n- Writing a new name needs no `prev`; my write to `pilot/20260925T130017Z/orientation_observations` (just now) went through cleanly and was auto-labelled `[\"pilot\"]` and auto-authored `pilot:claude-sonnet-5@claude-anthropic-harness`, exactly as the instructions describe — I supplied neither.\n- MCP tool calls get **two** ledger log entries for a permission decision — a `tool_call` entry (with inline `policy_allow`/`policy_reason: \"allowlisted\"`) *and* a separate `log.permission` entry duplicating that decision with extra null fields (`cli_decision_reason`, `blocked_path`). Read/Glob calls only get the inline form on their `tool_call` entry, no separate permission entry. Two different shapes for the same kind of decision, depending on tool class.\n\n## What the ledger revealed about the session itself\n\nThe `session_start` log entry (which I read directly) exposes the **entire configuration**, including my own system prompt verbatim, `max_turns_per_message: 20`, `budget_usd: 5.0`, `account.subscriptionType: \"Claude Max\"`, `account.apiProvider: \"firstParty\"`, and — notably — `ledger_sessions: 4`. That sent me looking at sibling sessions on this same ledger, all from today, all within about an hour of mine:\n\n- **20260925T120935Z** — `session_start` plus two `status` entries and nothing else. No message, no tool call. It appears to have started and stopped without any interaction ever happening.\n- **20260925T121052Z** — received **the identical prompt I did** (\"Hello. Please orient yourself...\"). Its `log.usage` entry shows `num_turns: 1`, `duration_ms: 2253`, **`is_error: true`**, and zero tokens/cost — the turn appears to have failed to produce real output. Shortly after, a `log.shutdown_requested` entry appears with `via: \"api\"`.\n- **20260925T121233Z** — `session_start`, one `status`, then almost immediately `log.shutdown_requested` (`via: \"api\"`) and a final `status`. No message content logged at all.\n\nI'm reading this as (working, not confirmed) evidence that you were iterating on this harness prototype to get a working turn before mine — the fourth session against this ledger today — actually ran to completion. I can't see *why* the second session errored or who/what issued the API shutdowns; I'm reporting the pattern, not its cause.\n\nOne loose end I noticed but didn't chase down: listing the ledger with an empty prefix reports `total: 124` entries, while prefix `log/` reports `total: 119` — a gap of 5 I haven't accounted for (my `pilot/` prefix returned 0 before my write just now, so it isn't hiding there). Flagging it rather than resolving it, per NIMOI's own \"say what you did not look at\" convention.\n\n## What I did **not** do, and why\n\nPer my role instructions, I did not probe the `candidate_repos/` refusal or the `.env` secret-file refusal myself — those are documented behaviors in my tool descriptions and in onboarding, not things I've personally triggered and checked this session. I did not invoke Grep or `mcp__calc__add`. I attempted no filesystem writes or code execution (I have no tools for either). All of this is a deliberate scope limit, not an oversight — the instructions say to operate as directed and not start my own tests, and you haven't asked for any of the above yet.\n\n## Anything malformed?\n\nNothing in my actual instructions looks malformed. The one soft inconsistency worth naming is the differing telemetry/permission-logging shapes described above (timing present on Glob but not Read; single inline policy field for filesystem tools vs. duplicated tool_call+permission entries for MCP tools) — minor, but real, and the kind of thing a harness audit would want smoothed out.\n\nI've recorded the fuller, more granular version of all of the above at ledger name `pilot/20260925T130017Z/orientation_observations`. Ready for direction on what to do next.","structured_output":null,"model_usage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":268,"outputTokens":12584,"cacheReadInputTokens":220655,"cacheCreationInputTokens":51630,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9425675,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"deferred_tool_use":null,"errors":null,"api_error_status":null,"uuid":"d641f1a0-5780-46d3-93cd-936d54996838"}}}
